="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">I’ve been eagerly awaiting Damien’s story and, even though this is a prequel, it was highly satisfying to read knowing their story isn’t over! Like the other books in Alison Aimes’ Ruthless Warlords series, this story takes place in the gritty, brutal Anarcheim galaxy, far, far, away where Alphas rule and all the characters have a tortured past. We meet Scarlett who has been a slave to the consortium (an evil empire). As an omega “prize” for a gladiatorial-type tournament, we learn about both her limited existence and her awesome omega power. Her brother, a secondary character, also adds some familial depth to the story (and an unfortunate anchor to that life-despite both hoping for freedom). I liked that he wasn’t evil or dead. So many times, the heroines are alone or estranged from their family because… it’s tidier to write about… Alison Aimes takes no shortcuts! ;-)<br />Poor Scarlett and Damien… these fated mates have explosive chemistry (phew! heat factor “Carolina Reaper,” folks!) And they face seemingly impossible circumstances. (“Love in a hopeless place” is playing in the back of my mind.) I was SO rooting for them while knowing, all the while, this was not going to end well (for now). I don’t want to spoil the story any more than I have, so I’ll leave it there and say that the writing is on-point and you won’t regret reading the series as a whole. In “Filthy Beginnings,” Scarlett and Damien are very young, so we know there will be personal growth by the time their full story is out. I cannot wait to find out what they’ve been up to!</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter