6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5927127879">October 23, 2023</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">This was a wonderful prequel to Filthy Royal. Stella Hunter and Jason Clarke always blow me away with their performances. Especially Jason in this one as there were many men that he had to do the voices for and I never had one issue with being able to tell who was talking. Jason also does the villain voices so so well. Stella can bring the emotions into a story perfectly and I am always in awe of her.<br /><br />Damien and Scarlett are definitely a forbidden love story. As she is being pushed into the direction of someone else but her heart belongs completely to Damien. Damien knows that he isn't the right man for her but the heart wants what the heart wants...and his is craving Scarlett. The pull that these two had for each other from the very beginning was palpable...you could feel it. <br /><br />With the way this one ended, I am immediately diving into Filthy Royal. I need to know how these two are going to find their way.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/26420298?shelf=alc" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">alc</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/26420298?shelf=audio-book" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">audio-book</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><foo